note right of Budget
  RunBudget enforces maxAgentCalls,
  maxTokens, maxEstimatedCostUsd and
  maxRevisions (fixed at 1); breaches
  raise HarnessError.
end note

note bottom of ITutorTool
  TutorTool validates its own input and
  result (validateInput / validateResult);
  ToolRegistryService adds retry, timeout,
  budget accounting and trace persistence.
end note

' ============================ FIGURE CAPTION ============================
' UML component view of the NestJS API's internal structure. Four thin controllers form the
' HTTP layer; CorpusController is the only one behind an authorisation guard
' (AdminIngestionKeyGuard), because ingestion is an operator function rather than a student
' one. TutorOrchestratorService is the single point that sequences a grounded run: it depends
' on the TutorRunStore interface for persistence, on HarnessPolicyService for its limits, on
' ToolRegistryService for tool access, and on four TutorAgent<TIn,TOut> implementations bound
' by injection token — ModelQueryTransformerAgent, DeterministicRetrievalAgent, ModelTutorAgent
' and ModelGroundingVerifierAgent. The agent and tool contracts are deliberately narrow and
' symmetric: an agent returns AgentResult<TOut> (output, token/cost usage, summary) and a tool
' returns ToolResult<TOut> while validating its own input and result, which lets the registry
' impose retries, timeouts, budget accounting and trace persistence uniformly on code it does
' not trust. Two structural points are worth noting because they differ from the obvious
' reading: retrieval is deterministic — DeterministicRetrievalAgent performs no model call and
' simply invokes the 'curriculum.search' tool with policy-supplied limit and threshold, so the
' only LLMs in a run are the transformer, tutor, verifier and translator; and RunBudget is not
' an injectable service but a per-run object constructed by the orchestrator, which is what
' makes its ceilings (agent calls, tokens, estimated cost, and a hard maxRevisions of 1)
' per-run rather than global. The ingestion pipeline (upload, storage, PDF extraction,
' chunking, embedding) runs off the request path via a BullMQ queue consumed by
' CorpusIngestionProcessor, and shares the EmbeddingProvider seam with query-time search.

@enduml
